# $name

One or two sentences: what this is, what it carries or holds, and where it
goes. Say "Not printed yet." while that is true.

![render](../../docs/img/$name.png)

## Status

`STATUS` in `params.py` says concept, passes, printed or parked. Here: what
passes, what is open, in two or three lines.

## Sources

Where the numbers come from: the standards, vendor sheets and board files
`params.py` cites, and which values are DESIGN choices or UNVERIFIED.
Anything unpublished and how the part tolerates it.

## Run

```
.venv/bin/python projects/$name/params.py     # prints the design
.venv/bin/python projects/$name/$name.py      # -> out/*.step, *.stl
.venv/bin/python -m pytest projects/$name
```

Long-form material (full parts list, spec, working log) goes in `NOTES.md` or
`SPEC.md`, not here. Keep this file under 80 lines.
